    "summary": "High‑energy Hawaii set with soaring Dark Star and blistering Lovelight",
    "blurb": "The show delivers a monster Dark Star, tight China Cat Sunflower > Rider flow and a fiery second half highlighted by The Other One and Turn On Your Lovelight. Jerry’s lead work is on fire while Pigpen commands Black Peter with vocal power. Soundboard recordings capture the crisp, clear mix for an essential listen.",
    "review": "January 23, 1970 at the Honolulu Civic Auditorium finds the Dead in top form, riding a wave of island‑inspired high energy that never lets up. The first half kicks off with a sparkling China Cat Sunflower → Rider segue, Pigpen’s gritty vocals on Black Peter and a spirited Hard To Handle that, while noted as uneven, adds raw charm. The second half erupts into a marathon Dark Star → Cryptical Envelopment → Dark Star sequence that feels both seamless and exploratory, before bursting into Saint Stephen and a blistering Turn On Your Lovelight where Jerry’s slide work soars. Throughout the set the band stays tightly locked, with tight transitions (China Cat Sunflower → Rider, The Other One) and a palpable Hawaiian vibe that lifts every improvisation. Both available soundboard sources are praised as crisp and well‑mixed, making this performance an essential snapshot of the Dead’s 1969‑era firepower.",
